---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';

const updated = 'September 19, 2026';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use & End-User Agreement | Koa’s Events"
  description="Terms of Use and End-User Agreement for the Koa’s Events website, client portals, proposals and online services."
  canonical="https://koasevents.com/terms/"
>
  <Header overlay={false} />
  <main class="bg-[var(--koa-ivory)] py-16 sm:py-20 lg:py-24">
    <article class="container-shell max-w-4xl">
      <p class="eyebrow text-[var(--koa-clay)]">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="display mt-4 text-5xl sm:text-6xl">Terms of Use & End-User Agreement</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-[var(--koa-ink)]/50">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-10 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--koa-ink)]/70">
        <section>
          <h2 class="display text-3xl text-[var(--koa-forest)]">1. Acceptance of these terms</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">These Terms of Use & End-User Agreement (“Terms”) apply to your use of koasevents.com and Koa’s Events online services, including inquiry forms, quote tools, proposal pages, booking pages, planning portals, and related administrative or client-facing features. By using these services, you agree to these Terms.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="display text-3xl text-[var(--koa-forest)]">2. Limited license to use the site and portals</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">Koa’s Events LLC grants you a limited, revocable, non-exclusive, non-transferable license to access and use the website and any portal made available to you for legitimate inquiry, booking, planning, event-management, or administrative purposes. You may not copy, resell, reverse engineer, scrape, interfere with, or misuse the website, its systems, private links, or administrative features.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="display text-3xl text-[var(--koa-forest)]">3. Website information, quotes and proposals</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">Website descriptions, availability information, quote-builder totals, package descriptions, rental quantities, and similar content are planning information and may be subject to final review. A saved quote or website estimate is not, by itself, a reservation or binding event contract.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">A proposal reflects the scope and pricing presented by Koa’s for the identified event. Your event is not considered fully booked solely because a proposal has been viewed or accepted. The booking requirements shown in your applicable agreement and payment schedule must also be completed.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="display text-3xl text-[var(--koa-forest)]">4. Event agreements control</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">If you enter into a venue rental agreement, mobile bar agreement, services agreement, proposal, change order, cancellation form, or other signed event document with Koa’s, that document governs the event-specific terms addressed in it. If these website Terms conflict with a signed event agreement, the signed event agreement controls for that event.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="display text-3xl text-[var(--koa-forest)]">5. QuickBooks estimates, invoices and payments</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">Koa’s uses QuickBooks Online for accounting workflows, including estimates, invoices, balances, and payment status. An estimate or invoice issued through QuickBooks is an accounting document associated with your Koa’s event or service. Payment instructions are provided through the QuickBooks workflow or other instructions expressly provided by Koa’s.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">The Koa’s website does not process payment-card information for QuickBooks payments. You remain responsible for paying amounts when due under your applicable proposal, invoice, agreement, or payment schedule.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="display text-3xl text-[var(--koa-forest)]">6. Secure booking and planning links</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">Booking and planning portals may be accessed through private links containing secure tokens. Treat those links as confidential. You are responsible for activity performed through a private link you share or expose to another person. Contact Koa’s if you believe a booking or planning link has been compromised.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="display text-3xl text-[var(--koa-forest)]">7. Information and files you provide</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">You are responsible for ensuring that information you submit is accurate and that you have the right to provide any uploaded file, image, floor plan, insurance certificate, vendor contact, or other content. You grant Koa’s permission to store, reproduce, transmit, and use submitted content as reasonably necessary to plan, administer, document, and deliver your event or requested services.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">Do not upload malicious code, unlawful content, payment-card data, passwords, government identification numbers, or other sensitive information that Koa’s has not specifically requested.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="display text-3xl text-[var(--koa-forest)]">8. Intellectual property</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">The Koa’s Events name, logos, branding, website design, copy, graphics, photographs owned or licensed by Koa’s, software features, and other site content are protected by applicable intellectual-property laws. Except for the limited right to use the website under these Terms, no rights are transferred to you.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="display text-3xl text-[var(--koa-forest)]">9. Acceptable use</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">You may not use the site or portals to violate law; impersonate another person; gain unauthorized access; probe or disrupt system security; introduce malware; abuse upload features; harvest information; send fraudulent requests; or interfere with the availability, integrity, or normal operation of the services.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="display text-3xl text-[var(--koa-forest)]">10. Third-party services</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">The website may connect to or rely on third-party services such as QuickBooks Online/Intuit and website infrastructure providers. Third-party services are also governed by their own terms and privacy practices. Koa’s is not responsible for a third party’s separate service, systems, or policies.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="display text-3xl text-[var(--koa-forest)]">11. Availability and changes</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">We may update, suspend, restrict, or discontinue website features, portal features, integrations, or content when reasonably necessary for maintenance, security, legal compliance, product changes, or business operations. We may also update these Terms from time to time. The “Last updated” date above identifies the current version.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="display text-3xl text-[var(--koa-forest)]">12. Disclaimer and limitation</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">Online tools are provided to support Koa’s event and service workflows. While we work to keep website information and records accurate, online services may occasionally contain errors, experience interruptions, or display information pending final staff or accounting review. To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, Koa’s will not be liable for indirect, incidental, special, exemplary, or consequential damages arising solely from use of or inability to use the website or online portals.</p>
          <p class="mt-3">Nothing in this section changes obligations or remedies expressly stated in a signed event agreement.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="display text-3xl text-[var(--koa-forest)]">13. Governing law</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of Hawaiʻi, without regard to conflict-of-law principles. Event-specific dispute provisions contained in a signed agreement remain controlling for that event.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2 class="display text-3xl text-[var(--koa-forest)]">14. Contact</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">Koa’s Events LLC<br />Mountain View, Hawaiʻi<br /><a class="underline" href="mailto:aloha@koasevents.com">aloha@koasevents.com</a><br /><a class="underline" href="tel:+18448085627">844-808-KOAS</a></p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
